Package: NordUniversityTemplates
Title: R Markdown Templates for Theses and Assignments at Nord University
Version: 1.0.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Nord University", "Business School", role = c("cph")),
    person("Thomas", "Leirvik", email = "thomas.leirvik@nord.no", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Provides modern R Markdown / bookdown templates for writing
    assignments, monography master theses, and article-based master theses
    at Nord University Business School. Templates use Times New Roman (an
    approved font for the master thesis) and the xelatex engine, and they
    compile cleanly on Windows, macOS and Linux without requiring any
    proprietary fonts.
Depends: R (>= 4.0.0)
Imports:
    knitr (>= 1.40),
    rmarkdown (>= 2.20),
    bookdown (>= 0.30),
    tinytex (>= 0.40),
    xfun (>= 0.35),
    yaml,
    tools,
    stringr
Suggests:
    devtools
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: true
RoxygenNote: 7.2.3
SystemRequirements:
    A working LaTeX installation (TinyTeX is recommended; install with
    tinytex::install_tinytex()). Pandoc >= 2.11. Either the Times New Roman
    font (preinstalled on Windows and macOS) OR the LaTeX packages
    'newtx' and 'fontspec' (installed automatically by TinyTeX on demand).
